  "pipeline": {
    "source": "Linux x86-64 Blender 5.2.2 LTS. Source blend archives embed their images. Original high library images also resolve from the model folder.",
    "bake": "Cycles CPU, final triangulated receiver, 2048x2048, isolated matched parts, selected-to-active tangent NORMAL and unlit EMIT. Assembled contact AO uses 12 rays and a 26 mm range. Independent receiver material corrects adjacent-face projections over 12 degrees.",
    "maps": "KTX-Software 4.4.2, glTF-compatible UASTC and Zstandard, all 12 mip levels. Four map payloads and four matching PNG fallbacks embedded.",
    "validation": "make model-check with RIFT_MODEL_CHECK_KTX explicitly set. Seven tests passed. Core and shared-library manifests passed decoded RGBA8, normal basis, finite UV area, exact role binding, planar normal and coplanar overlap checks.",
    "views": "Blender 5.2.2 EEVEE on Apple Silicon, 24 samples, 768x768 fixed paired front/isometric/detail/underside. Low views use actual re-imported GLB and the decoded KTX2 level zero. Motion uses 12 overhead samples at 384x384.",
    "determinism": "Two Linux source runs matched all four uncompressed bakes, geometry measurements, source glTF JSON and binary. A clean re-encode and repack matched all four KTX2s, registered manifest and GLB byte-for-byte. Blender archive hashes identify the retained editable files."
  },
  "corrections": [
    "Visual review tightened the prism, darkened the side cassettes and restored the paired shoulder ribs and recessed service cover seen in the design.",
    "The initial compressed normal contained eight sub-threshold vector lengths. The corrected receiver-aware bake replaced the steep cross-seam projections before compression.",
    "Sampled Blender re-import exposed uneven cubic quaternion interpolation. The final editable source uses a linear axial turn and exports sampled rotation. The imported half-second position measures 22.5 degrees and the eight-second turn returns to neutral."
  ],
